From: gemini-nixos (phase-4 desktop port)
Date: 2026-09-07
Subject: backend/libinput: handle LIBINPUT_SWITCH_KEYPAD_SLIDE (libinput >= 1.28)

wlroots 0.18.2 predates libinput 1.28, which added the
LIBINPUT_SWITCH_KEYPAD_SLIDE switch type. Under the pin's libinput
(1.31.x) the switch statement in handle_switch_toggle misses that
enumeration value and wlroots' default -Werror turns it into a build
failure (enumeration value not handled in switch). There is no
WLR_SWITCH_TYPE for it in the 0.18 API, so drop the event instead of
emitting a garbage-typed toggle.

Only meaningful when built against libinput >= 1.28 (always the case in
this repo: the nixpkgs pin carries libinput 1.31.3). Upstream wlroots
fixed this the same way on later versions.

--- a/backend/libinput/switch.c
+++ b/backend/libinput/switch.c
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@ void handle_switch_toggle(struct libinput_event *event,
 	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_TABLET_MODE:
 		wlr_event.switch_type = WLR_SWITCH_TYPE_TABLET_MODE;
 		break;
+	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_KEYPAD_SLIDE:
+		/* libinput >= 1.28 added this after wlroots 0.18 shipped;
+		 * no WLR_SWITCH_TYPE for it — drop the event. */
+		return;
 	}
 	switch (libinput_event_switch_get_switch_state(sevent)) {
 	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_STATE_OFF:
